# index.html is a generated deploy artifact, never hand-edited - it's an
# exact copy of kaizen_raid_manager.html (the real source file), made by
# `npm run deploy:frontend` right before every deploy. It used to be
# tracked in git as its own file, which is exactly how it silently
# drifted out of sync with kaizen_raid_manager.html for an entire session
# (2026-09-10) - every commit in that arc was real and correct, but the
# live site kept serving this file's stale, untouched copy the whole
# time. Untracking it removes the possibility of that drift recurring;
# it's regenerated fresh on every deploy, so it never needs to be a
# source file at all. See CHANGELOG.md's top entry.
index.html
